{"id": "tea:naresvarapariksa:1", "source": "src:naresvarapariksa", "location": {"ref": "1", "chapter": "prakaraṇa 1"}, "paraphrase": "Against the Buddhists and materialists, there is a permanent soul distinct from body, senses and cognitions: recognition, memory and the unity of experience require a lasting knower whose consciousness is its own nature.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "dispute"], "disputes": ["dsp:is-there-a-self"], "terms": ["trm:pasu"], "teachers": ["tch:sadyojyoti"], "notes": "Chapter- or work-level reference; exact verse not given.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:naresvarapariksa:2", "source": "src:naresvarapariksa", "location": {"ref": "2", "chapter": "prakaraṇa 2 (low confidence)"}, "paraphrase": "Souls are many, not one: their experiences, bondage and release differ, and one soul's release does not release all.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "dispute"], "disputes": ["dsp:souls-one-or-distinct"], "notes": "Chapter- or work-level reference; exact verse not given.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:naresvarapariksa:3", "source": "src:naresvarapariksa", "location": {"ref": "3", "chapter": "prakaraṇa 3"}, "paraphrase": "The unconscious māyā and karma cannot organize themselves to give each soul its due fruits; an omniscient, omnipotent Lord, distinct from souls, must be their director — as the potter is of clay.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["ultimate", "dispute"], "disputes": ["dsp:isvara"], "terms": ["trm:pati", "trm:nimitta-karana"], "teachers": ["tch:sadyojyoti"], "notes": "Chapter- or work-level reference; exact verse not given. Chapter numbering low confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
